  "description": "SEPBIC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H80 N8 O22 Tb4,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.671-4.171 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.69-129.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C58H88Tb4N8O24. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
